  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,&nbsp;plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>,</p><p>Whose normal vector is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8801;</mo><msub><mover><mi>n</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Second plane,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>,</p><p>Whose normal vector is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8801;</mo><msub><mover><mi>n</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now let plane perpendicular to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;will have normal vector&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi>n</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>Where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi>n</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mover><mi>n</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mover><mi>n</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mover><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd><mtd><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd><mtd><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi>n</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Equation of plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math>&nbsp;through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi>n</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;as normal vector will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi>E</mi></math></p><p>Now distance of point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p>Now given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now distance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>21</mn></msqrt><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
